A||||9||jerpro||Damn Air!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||jerpro||01-23-2001||09:18 PM||||I was riding back from work yesterday and while I rested my knee on the door handle mechanism (on the inside) I could feel air coming into the car from it. IT happens when I have my sunroof open (don't ask why I open it in grand rapids michigan, long story) Is this common in 84's? is there a simple way of fixing it?<P>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if at first you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||01-23-2001||09:22 PM||||There are a number of ways air get's thru the door. you probably feel it more with the roof open because you are creating a slight vacuum in the car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||01-23-2001||09:31 PM||||in 11 years of ownership, i have always felt air coming in around the door handles.<P>dont know why, dont know if i really care... it kinda balances out the heat coming up from those cooling pipes underneath my a$$<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000003||firstfiero||01-23-2001||11:11 PM||||I feel the same thing....do you guys notice that your feet FREEZE!!! in a fiero. Must be because Theirs no heat coming through the fire wall.....86se||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||01-24-2001||12:47 AM||||Actually, heat does come through the firewall.  Just from the opposite direction.. After driving for awhile, feel your ashtrays, or take them out and stick you fingers down into the console.  Can get pretty warm down there.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||01-24-2001||01:03 AM||||The air is supposed to come through there. It is part of the vent system for the car.<P>Try this - as you are driving and feel the air, crack your window just a bit. As soon as air starts coming in the window, you stop feeling it at the door handle. It will also stop when you turn on the heat or A/C.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||01-24-2001||11:43 AM||||I was always under the impression that it was warm air getting pulled through the holes in the firewall for the shift cables, wiring harness etc.  Now that I think about it, it was always most noticable when I had the sunroof off.  I know there's vents for the ECM on the sides of the console behind the seats.  And I don't think a car company would actually design a car to pull in air from the engine compartment, which could contain some interesting fumes.. of course, I could be wrong.<P>On a side note, ever wonder why it's so loud inside the car when you have the sunroof off at freeway speeds?  Because the air resonates at the frequency of a human head  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  forgot which web site I saw that on...||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tigger||01-24-2001||12:13 PM||||Also don't forget the air vents behind the sail panels.  That type of vent can be found in the door jams on on other cars.  My '85 Regal has them.<P>I believe there's some sort of government requirement or whatnot for a minimum amount of ventilation inside the cabin on all production cars.  Notice on all new Chevrolet/GMC suburbans, blazers, full size vans have visible vents on the rear pillars.  Yuk yuk...  <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 01-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||bHooper||01-24-2001||02:44 PM||||if you pull the molding back, on the pillar's, you will find a special hanger located there for the pine tree air freshener!<P>that was a well thought out design, by gm!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||01-24-2001||05:48 PM||||i get air blowing in thru the inside handle openings too. Mine is because I left off the sheet of paper thats supposed to cover the whole inside of door under the inside panel.||||reg||1
